`]}),e.jsxs(n,{title:"One latent feeds the keys and values of every head",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["DeepSeek-V2 introduced multi-head latent attention (MLA), which compresses the key-value state of each token into one content latent that every head shares ",e.jsx(a,{id:"deepseekv2",children:"DeepSeek-AI, 2024"}),". We use two of DeepSeek-V2's symbols: ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_h",display:!1})," for the head width, the course's ",e.jsx(s,{math:"D_h",display:!1}),", and ",e.jsx(s,{math:"n_h",display:!1})," for the number of query heads, the course's ",e.jsx(s,{math:"H",display:!1}),". We write the number of KV heads as ",e.jsx(s,{math:"n_{kv}",display:!1}),", the course's ",e.jsx(s,{math:"H_{kv}",display:!1})," and the exercise's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"n_kv_heads"}),". The rotary width is ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_r",display:!1}),", as in the exercise, where DeepSeek-V2 writes ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_h^R",display:!1}),". Vectors are columns, ",e.jsx(s,{math:"h_t",display:!1})," is the hidden state of token ",e.jsx(s,{math:"t",display:!1})," entering the attention layer, of width ",e.jsx(s,{math:"D",display:!1}),", and ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_c",display:!1})," is the width of the latent. A subscript ",e.jsx(s,{math:"h",display:!1})," on a matrix or a key indexes the head."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["MLA rests on a shared latent and per-head up-projections. A down-projection ",e.jsx(s,{math:"W^{DKV}",display:!1}),", a ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_c \\times D",display:!1})," matrix that all heads share, maps the hidden state to the latent, and each head ",e.jsx(s,{math:"h",display:!1})," has two up-projections ",e.jsx(s,{math:"W^{UK}_h",display:!1})," and ",e.jsx(s,{math:"W^{UV}_h",display:!1}),", each a ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_h \\times d_c",display:!1})," matrix, that define its content key and content value:"]}),e.jsx(s,{math:"c_t^{KV} = W^{DKV} h_t, \\qquad k^C_{t,h} = W^{UK}_h c_t^{KV}, \\qquad v^C_{t,h} = W^{UV}_h c_t^{KV}."}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Stacking the up-projections of all ",e.jsx(s,{math:"n_h",display:!1})," heads, one block of ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_h",display:!1})," rows per head, gives two matrices ",e.jsx(s,{math:"W^{UK}",display:!1})," and ",e.jsx(s,{math:"W^{UV}",display:!1}),", each ",e.jsx(s,{math:"n_h d_h \\times d_c",display:!1}),". Applied to the latent, they give the content keys and the content values of all heads at once, which is how DeepSeek-V2 writes the definitions ",e.jsx(a,{id:"deepseekv2",children:"DeepSeek-AI, 2024"}),":"]}),e.jsx(s,{math:"k^C_t = W^{UK} c_t^{KV}, \\qquad v^C_t = W^{UV} c_t^{KV}."}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Each is ",e.jsx(s,{math:"n_h d_h",display:!1})," wide, and head ",e.jsx(s,{math:"h",display:!1}),"'s key ",e.jsx(s,{math:"k^C_{t,h}",display:!1})," and value ",e.jsx(s,{math:"v^C_{t,h}",display:!1})," are its ",e.jsx(s,{math:"h",display:!1}),"-th block of ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_h",display:!1})," coordinates."]}),e.jsx(t.h4,{children:"Keys and values share one low-rank compression"}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Substituting the latent writes the keys of all heads as ",e.jsx(s,{math:"k^C_t = W^{UK} W^{DKV} h_t",display:!1}),". The product ",e.jsx(s,{math:"W^{UK} W^{DKV}",display:!1})," is an ",e.jsx(s,{math:"n_h d_h \\times D",display:!1})," matrix, the same shape as the key projection of multi-head attention. Every vector it produces passes through the ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_c",display:!1})," coordinates of the latent, so the product has rank at most ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_c",display:!1}),'. The values pass through the same latent. DeepSeek-V2 calls this "the low-rank joint compression for keys and values" and names it the core of MLA ',e.jsx(a,{id:"deepseekv2",children:"DeepSeek-AI, 2024"}),". The compression is low-rank because the latent is narrow, and joint because one latent serves both keys and values."]}),e.jsx(t.h4,{children:"DeepSeek-V2's widths and weights"}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Two assumptions fix the numbers."}),e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
