`]}),e.jsx(n,{title:"Two designs on one template",children:e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["DSA and MSA both learn where exact attention should look, and both run the same four stages: index, select, read, and exact attention over the selected set. They differ in what they select, tokens or blocks, and in who shares a selection, all heads or each GQA group. Both descend from Native Sparse Attention (NSA) ",e.jsx(a,{id:"yuan2025",children:"Yuan et al., 2025"}),". Week 8 turns to hybrid attention, which interleaves linear and full attention layers."]})})]}),e.jsxs(i,{title:"DeepSeek's global KV cache per token shrank 437-fold since 2023",reading:!0,accent:5,number:"47",children:[e.jsx(v,{}),e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
