`]}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The third is the full-context reference against which both windowed numbers are read. It lets every query see its whole prefix, so it holds the scored tokens fixed but not the cache size. The text, tokenizer, model, slice, scoring positions and seed stay fixed, and the window and the sink positions come from the trace, so only the retained positions differ between the two windowed numbers."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The provided harness calls your evaluation again for two controls and a sweep. The first control retains as many random positions as there are sinks, which tests whether any extra column helps or only the sink positions do. The second narrows the window by the number of sinks and retains the sinks, so its cache is the same size as the window alone. The sweep repeats the window-only and with-sinks perplexities at windows of 64, 128, 256 and 512. The exercise trains no sink and runs no eviction loop. Each perplexity comes from one forward pass under a mask, so neither windowed number describes a serving policy."}),e.jsx(t.h4,{children:"MLA, unabsorbed"}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The third result is MLA in its unabsorbed form, a second attention class beside Week 3's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"CausalSelfAttention"}),". Its latent width ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_c",display:!1})," and its rotary width ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_r",display:!1})," are configurable, and ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_r",display:!1})," must be even. You count the ",e.jsx(s,{math:"d_c + d_r",display:!1})," elements that each token stores per layer, reconstruct every head's content key and value from the latent, and test causality, the shapes and the cache-element arithmetic. The cache holds only the stored elements, so the reconstructed per-head keys and values do not count toward it."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(i,{title:"Exercise: Measurements Need Named Boundaries",reading:!0,accent:2,number:"52",items:"6",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
